[agent:result] DESCRIPTION
[agent:result]     This command will attempt to run the custom job immediately upon creation.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] EXAMPLES
[agent:result]     To create a job under project example in region us-central1, run:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]         $ gcloud ai custom-jobs create --region=us-central1 \
[agent:result]             --project=example \
[agent:result]             --worker-pool-spec=replica-count=1,machine-type='n1-highmem-2',\
[agent:result]         container-image-uri='gcr.io/ucaip-test/ucaip-training-test' \
[agent:result]             --display-name=test
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] REQUIRED FLAGS
[agent:result]      --display-name=DISPLAY_NAME
[agent:result]         Display name of the custom job to create.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]      Worker pool specification.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]      At least one of these must be specified:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]        --config=CONFIG
[agent:result]           Path to the job configuration file. This file should be a YAML
[agent:result]           document containing a `CustomJobSpec`
[agent:result]           (https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/reference/rest/v1/CustomJobSpec).
[agent:result]           If an option is specified both in the configuration file **and** via
[agent:result]           command-line arguments, the command-line arguments override the
[agent:result]           configuration file. Note that keys with underscore are invalid.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]           Example(YAML):
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]               workerPoolSpecs:
[agent:result]                 machineSpec:
[agent:result]                   machineType: n1-highmem-2
[agent:result]                 replicaCount: 1
[agent:result]                 containerSpec:
[agent:result]                   imageUri: gcr.io/ucaip-test/ucaip-training-test
[agent:result]                   args:
[agent:result]                   - port=8500
[agent:result]                   command:
[agent:result]                   - start
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]        --worker-pool-spec=[WORKER_POOL_SPEC,...]
[agent:result]           Define the worker pool configuration used by the custom job. You can
[agent:result]           specify multiple worker pool specs in order to create a custom job
[agent:result]           with multiple worker pools.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]           The spec can contain the following fields:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]            machine-type
[agent:result]               (Required): The type of the machine. see
[agent:result]               https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/training/configure-compute#machine-types
[agent:result]               for supported types. This is corresponding to the
[agent:result]               machineSpec.machineType field in WorkerPoolSpec API message.
[agent:result]            replica-count
[agent:result]               The number of worker replicas to use for this worker pool, by
[agent:result]               default the value is 1. This is corresponding to the replicaCount
[agent:result]               field in WorkerPoolSpec API message.
[agent:result]            accelerator-type
[agent:result]               The type of GPUs. see
[agent:result]               https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/training/configure-compute#specifying_gpus
[agent:result]               for more requirements. This is corresponding to the
[agent:result]               machineSpec.acceleratorType field in WorkerPoolSpec API message.
[agent:result]            accelerator-count
[agent:result]               The number of GPUs for each VM in the worker pool to use, by
[agent:result]               default the value if 1. This is corresponding to the
[agent:result]               machineSpec.acceleratorCount field in WorkerPoolSpec API message.
[agent:result]            container-image-uri
[agent:result]               The URI of a container image to be directly run on each worker
[agent:result]               replica. This is corresponding to the containerSpec.imageUri
[agent:result]               field in WorkerPoolSpec API message.
[agent:result]            executor-image-uri
[agent:result]               The URI of a container image that will run the provided package.
[agent:result]            output-image-uri
[agent:result]               The URI of a custom container image to be built for autopackaged
[agent:result]               custom jobs.
[agent:result]            python-module
[agent:result]               The Python module name to run within the provided package.
[agent:result]            local-package-path
[agent:result]               The local path of a folder that contains training code.
[agent:result]            script
[agent:result]               The relative path under the local-package-path to a file to
[agent:result]               execute. It can be a Python file or an arbitrary bash script.
[agent:result]            requirements
[agent:result]               Python dependencies to be installed from PyPI, separated by ";".
[agent:result]               This is supposed to be used when some public packages are
[agent:result]               required by your training application but not in the base images.
[agent:result]               It has the same effect as editing a "requirements.txt" file under
[agent:result]               local-package-path.
[agent:result]            extra-packages
[agent:result]               Relative paths of local Python archives to be installed,
[agent:result]               separated by ";". This is supposed to be used when some custom
[agent:result]               packages are required by your training application but not in the
[agent:result]               base images. Every path should be relative to the
[agent:result]               local-package-path.
[agent:result]            extra-dirs
[agent:result]               Relative paths of the folders under local-package-path to be
[agent:result]               copied into the container, separated by ";". If not specified,
[agent:result]               only the parent directory that contains the main executable
[agent:result]               (script or python-module) will be copied.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]           Note that some of these fields are used for different job creation
[agent:result]           methods and are categorized as mutually exclusive groups listed
[agent:result]           below. Exactly one of these groups of fields must be specified:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]            container-image-uri
[agent:result]               Specify this field to use a custom container image for training.
[agent:result]               Together with the --command and --args flags, this field
[agent:result]               represents a `WorkerPoolSpec.ContainerSpec`
[agent:result]               (https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/reference/rest/v1/CustomJobSpec?#containerspec)
